  <entry>
    <id>urn:singine:cleanup:gov:gov-001</id>
    <title>GOV-001 — Response Transparency</title>
    <updated>2026-05-23T13:31:35Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://singine.uk/cleanup.html#governance"/>
    <category term="governance"/>
    <category term="gov-001"/>
    <content type="text">Applies: Every time a human selects a response option

Rule: The selection MUST be recorded in the audit log with actor, timestamp, question ID, and chosen position before any action is dispatched. No action may begin without a confirmed audit entry.</content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>urn:singine:cleanup:gov:gov-002</id>
    <title>GOV-002 — Sync Action Accountability</title>
    <updated>2026-05-23T13:31:35Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://singine.uk/cleanup.html#governance"/>
    <category term="governance"/>
    <category term="gov-002"/>
    <content type="text">Applies: Every synchronous action execution

Rule: Sync actions execute in the same thread as the response. Result (success or error) MUST be written to audit log and executions table. On failure the session continues; it does not abort remaining sync actions.</content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>urn:singine:cleanup:gov:gov-003</id>
    <title>GOV-003 — Async Action Queuing</title>
    <updated>2026-05-23T13:31:35Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://singine.uk/cleanup.html#governance"/>
    <category term="governance"/>
    <category term="gov-003"/>
    <content type="text">Applies: Every asynchronous action dispatch

Rule: Async actions are enqueued in SQLite (status=pending). A singine worker polls and executes them independently. The enqueue operation is synchronous; the execution is not. Idempotency keys MUST be set on every async payload.</content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>urn:singine:cleanup:gov:gov-004</id>
    <title>GOV-004 — Human Task Escalation</title>
    <updated>2026-05-23T13:31:35Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://singine.uk/cleanup.html#governance"/>
    <category term="governance"/>
    <category term="gov-004"/>
    <content type="text">Applies: Any action whose type is "human"

Rule: A human_tasks record is created (status=open) and a notification is sent (webhook or email). The session that triggered the task does NOT wait for resolution. Human tasks MUST be resolved within the configured SLA window (default: 48 h). Unresolved tasks after SLA are re-notified.</content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>urn:singine:cleanup:gov:gov-005</id>
    <title>GOV-005 — Logseq Sync Integrity</title>
    <updated>2026-05-23T13:31:35Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://singine.uk/cleanup.html#governance"/>
    <category term="governance"/>
    <category term="gov-005"/>
    <content type="text">Applies: Any push or pull between local state and Logseq

Rule: A content hash of each page/block is stored before and after sync. On hash mismatch without an explicit commit, the sync is aborted and recorded as a conflict in audit log.</content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>urn:singine:cleanup:gov:gov-006</id>
    <title>GOV-006 — Knowledge Base Immutability</title>
    <updated>2026-05-23T13:31:35Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://singine.uk/cleanup.html#governance"/>
    <category term="governance"/>
    <category term="gov-006"/>
    <content type="text">Applies: Any mutation to questions or response options

Rule: Questions and responses are versioned, not edited in place. The previous version is retained and marked inactive. All executions reference the version active at the time of the response.</content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>urn:singine:cleanup:gov:gov-007</id>
    <title>GOV-007 — Cost Visibility</title>
    <updated>2026-05-23T13:31:35Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://singine.uk/cleanup.html#governance"/>
    <category term="governance"/>
    <category term="gov-007"/>
    <content type="text">Applies: Any response option with costLevel ≥ "high"

Rule: Before dispatching actions, the CLI MUST display the cost level and list all actions that will be triggered. An explicit confirmation prompt is required. Auto-mode (non-interactive) is not permitted for "critical" cost actions without a governance override flag.</content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>urn:singine:cleanup:gov:gov-008</id>
    <title>GOV-008 — silkpage Content Transformation Traceability</title>
    <updated>2026-05-23T13:31:35Z</updated>
    <link rel="alternate" href="https://singine.uk/cleanup.html#governance"/>
    <category term="governance"/>
    <category term="gov-008"/>
    <content type="text">Applies: Any content transformation via silkpage

Rule: Input and output content hashes, the transformation template name, and silkpage version MUST be logged. Transformed content is stored in a staging area; it does not replace source until a commit step.</content>
  </entry>
